The `useSidebar` hook returns safe default values when used outside its provider. While this prevents crashes, it can silently hide bugs where a provider is missing but expected. A more robust pattern for required contexts is to throw an error. The existing `useSidebarOptional` hook already serves the use case for optional consumption. I recommend modifying `useSidebar` to enforce the presence of its provider.

