![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The headed mode for Chromium uses a fixed 60-second timeout before closing the browser, which is inconsistent with the Firefox launch logic that waits for user input. This can lead to a poor user experience if the browser closes unexpectedly. A better approach is to wait for the user to manually close the browser window.

```suggestion
    if (!$headless_flag) {
        console.log('Browser is open. Close the browser window to exit the script.');
        await new Promise(resolve => browser.on('close', resolve));
    } else {
        await browser.close();
    }
```

