![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The loop to scroll and load assets is hardcoded to 3 iterations. This might not be sufficient to load all desired assets on a slow connection, or it might perform unnecessary scrolls. A more robust approach would be to scroll in a loop until no new assets are loaded, or a desired count is reached.

For example:
```javascript
let previousAssetCount = 0;
let currentAssetCount = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) { // Max 10 scrolls
  await page.evaluate(() => window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight));
  await page.waitForTimeout(1500); // Wait for content to load
  currentAssetCount = await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelectorAll('main img').length);
  if (currentAssetCount === previousAssetCount) {
    break; // No new assets loaded
  }
  previousAssetCount = currentAssetCount;
}
```

