![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

This pattern of locating a button, checking if it exists, force-clicking it, and logging is now duplicated in 10 places across this file. To improve maintainability and adhere to the Don't Repeat Yourself (DRY) principle, I recommend abstracting this logic into a helper function.

You could define a helper function, for example:
```javascript
async function forceClickButton(page, { locator, logMessage }) {
  const button = page.locator(locator);
  if (await button.count() > 0) {
    await button.first().click({ force: true });
    console.log(logMessage);
  }
}
```

Then, this block and the other 9 instances could be replaced by a single call:
```javascript
await forceClickButton(page, {
  locator: 'button:has-text("Generate"), button:has-text("Create"), button:has-text("Apply"), button[type="submit"]:visible',
  logMessage: 'Clicked generate/apply button'
});
```
This refactoring would make the code cleaner and easier to manage in the future.
